-- WoW Forever: Blizzard's live hotfix records for 108 items whose stats on our realm differ from live (the 2026-11-23 item
-- comparison against MythicSim's live item list: 136 of the 362 differing items have a live ItemSparse record). Records from the
-- public mirror of the live hotfix file (https://storage.googleapis.com/raidbots-static/wow/forever/enUS/DBCache.bin, read
-- 2026-11-23, build 71037), Blizzard's values unchanged: Item and ItemSparse (108 each), ItemSearchName (106) and 10
-- ItemModifiedAppearance rows of those items. The records are from pushes 112623-114147.
-- Layouts: the cache is build 71037 and the server reads 70959 layouts. WoWDBDefs lists 70959 and 71037 under the same layout
-- for Item (9A2A4834) and ItemSparse (6FCC3191), and every record decodes to its exact size; a spot check against the client's
-- 70959 ItemSparse rows lines up field by field.
-- What our rows were: 68 from the beta sniff 70124 (2026_10_01_02), 10 with 1.12 values (2026_10_31_95), 20 with no hotfix row
-- (the client's own row, which live overrides), 10 from older live captures. 84 of the 108 have no row in the client's 70959
-- ItemSparse at all, so live sends them only through these records.
-- Each record is the item's newest record up to push 114196. Left out: items with a record after push 114196 (10 Grovekeeper and
-- Spiritcaller pieces, changed again by later pushes: the import of every newer push brings them); records live marks invalid (status 3: 18 Marshal
-- / General / Warlord PvP set pieces that live hides from clients, not changes to them); and, as in every earlier import,
-- the per-item shop pushes above 16 million (for these 108 items they hold the same bytes as the regular record taken here).
-- At the end: 11 server-only spell power effects from 2026_11_22_70 removed, since these records now carry that power as stats.
-- Made with live_hotfix_sql.py (--records, --max-push 114196, --statuses 1,2), taking each record's newest push inside the window.
-- hotfix_data ids 2116000-2116331. Safe to run again.

